From 5285f6b2c099dcfcbc0adb5ae359bbe437aee72a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan McDonald <ryan.mcdonald@bit-bud.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 05:33:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Make grok worker-selectable: agent.provider grok on the
 claude-tier trust path
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Stage 2 of the Grok Build host: the local autonomy worker can now drive
grok. The change is deliberately an enum-and-docs change, because every
provider branch in the worker is written as === 'codex' — grok lands on
the claude side of each one, which is the correct tier: its harness
enforces the role's --allow rules at run time (headless refuses un-ruled
calls) and performs its own git, both verified against xai-org/grok-build
sources, so no containment tiers, state snapshots, or capability
acknowledgements apply.

- autonomy.cjs + schemas/autonomy.schema.json: provider enums gain 'grok'
  (base and per-role); the codex-only knob guards already reject
  sandbox/approval/containment_tier/acknowledged_enforcement_gaps for any
  non-codex provider, grok included.
- agent-exec.cjs / worker/index.cjs: usage strings and comments name the
  third provider.
- README host matrix: grok local-autonomy column flips to Supported;
  QUICKSTART gains the minimal provider: grok autonomy.yml and the cost
  note (API-key traffic stamps real cost; a subscription login may report
  UNKNOWN, handled by limits.unknown_cost_behavior). Actions autonomy
  stays deferred.
- tests/agents-grok.test.cjs: four new tests — provider grok validates
  (base + per-role), the codex-only knobs stay rejected under grok,
  autonomous grok needs no containment tier while the codex tier-2 gate
  is untouched, and resolveEffectiveAgent resolves a per-role grok
  override.
